Instructions retired on the guest, marker overhead subtracted.
Deterministic per environment: -icount shift=0 pins one instruction to
one tick, so the same ELF under the same QEMU build yields the same
counts on any host. Different QEMU builds can shift region boundaries
by an instruction -- compare inside the reference image (verify.sh).

